**IoC** — the framework controls object creation and wiring instead of the application code.

Spring implements IoC via the **IoC Container** (ApplicationContext):

1. You define beans (via `@Component`, `@Service`, `@Bean`, etc.)
2. Spring instantiates, configures, and manages their lifecycle
3. Dependencies are **injected** — not `new`-ed by the caller

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
  private final PaymentService payment; // injected
  public OrderService(PaymentService p) { this.payment = p; }
}
```
